# Cloud packages

- Cloud packages must not import each other (import-linter enforces it).
- Depend on `crc.core` only; do not reach into `crc.py`.
- Each resource implements `plan()` (read-only) and `apply()` (mutating) and is
  registered with the registry decorator once `crc/core` exists.
- Inject SDK clients; do not build them at import time.
- Destructive resources need a real age gate; fail closed on bad age, tags or
  telemetry. Keep destructive call order from `CLEANUP_SAFETY.md`.
- Do not catch broad `Exception` silently. Catch specific SDK errors, log the
  resource id, chain with `raise ... from e`.
- No extra retry layer on top of SDK retries.
- Legacy modules are listed in `pyproject.toml`; when you refactor one, remove
  it from the lists. Never add one.
- Tests mock the SDK; never call a real cloud API.
